<title>PORTUGAL: BPI estimates BFE 'goodwill' at 39 bln esc.</title>
<headline>BPI estimates BFE 'goodwill' at 39 bln esc.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco Portugues de Investimento said it paid 39 billion escudos ($253.5 million) in 'goodwill' in its purchase of Banco de Fomento &amp; Exterior.</p>
<p>&quot;The goodwill is the difference between the price to pay for 100 percent of BFE (209 billion escudos) and the average net worth of BFE (170 billion),&quot; the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>An extraordinary meeting of BPI shareholders approved on Wednesday a 21.5 billion escudo capital rise to pay for the purchase.</p>
<p>BPI agreed to buy state-controlled Banco de Fomento e Exterior in August.</p>
<p>($1=153.844)</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3113126</p>
</text>
